    <!-- ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
         DEFAULT BANK LAYOUTS FOR CHECK PRINTING
         ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

         Coordinate system:
           Origin (0,0) = top-left of the check paper.
           X increases to the right, Y increases downward.
           All values in mm.

         These are representative starting-point coordinates.
         Because physical check dimensions vary by batch, users MUST use
         the "Test Print" feature (PDC Management → Config → Bank Print Layouts
         → action_test_print) to calibrate their actual check stock.

         Approach: print a calibration sheet on plain A4, overlay with the
         actual check, mark the desired field positions, then update X/Y values.

         ── Egyptian banks ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
         Egyptian standard business checks are typically 220 mm × 96 mm,
         printed landscape, with pre-printed Arabic field labels.

         ── Saudi banks ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
         Saudi standard business checks follow SAMA layout guidelines:
         220 mm × 100 mm landscape. Fields appear in both Arabic (right) and
         English (left). The layouts below target the Arabic field zones.

         Sources: bank specimen checks published by each bank + community
         measurements. Treat as a calibration starting point, not exact.
    ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════ -->

